le</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Antifungal combinations against <italic>Candida albicans</italic> biofilms in vitro</article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</source><year>2003</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>3657</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14576141</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Baddley</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Pappas</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Antifungal combination therapy: clinical potential</article-title><source>Drugs</source><year>2005</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>1461</fpage><lpage>80</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16033288</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Balashov</surname><given-names>SV</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Perlin</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessing resistance to the echinocandin antifungal drug caspofungin in <italic>Candida albicans</italic> by profiling mutations in <italic>FKS1</italic></article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</source><year>2006</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>2058</fpage><lpage>63</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16723566</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barchiesi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Spreghini</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Tomassetti</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Effects of caspofungin against <italic>Candida guilliermondii</italic> and <italic>Candida parapsilosis</italic></article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</so